				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body" aria-labelledby="firstHeading" data-mw-ve-target-container>
					<div class="vector-body-before-content">
							<div class="mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div>
					</div>
					<div id="contentSub"><div id="mw-content-subtitle"></div></div>
					
					
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-subjectpageheader">
</div><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha18" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Process of extending a representation of a subgroup to the parent group"}},"i":0}}]}'>Process of extending a representation of a subgroup to the parent group</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_with_empty_Wikidata_description"/></span>

<p id="mwAw">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_theory" title="Group theory" id="mwBA">group theory</a>, the <b id="mwBQ">induced representation</b> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_representation" title="Group representation" id="mwBg">representation of a group</a>, <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt2" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span>, which is constructed using a known representation of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subgroup" title="Subgroup" id="mwCA">subgroup</a> <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt3" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span>. Given a representation of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt4" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span><i id="mwCw">,</i> the induced representation is, in a sense, the "most general" representation of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt5" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> that extends the given one. Since it is often easier to find representations of the smaller group <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt6" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span> than of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt7" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span><i id="mwDw">,</i> the operation of forming induced representations is an important tool to construct new representations<i id="mwEA">.</i></p>

<p id="mwEQ">Induced representations were initially defined by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_Georg_Frobenius" title="Ferdinand Georg Frobenius" id="mwEg">Frobenius</a>, for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear_representation" title="Linear representation" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEw">linear representations</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finite_group" title="Finite group" id="mwFA">finite groups</a>. The idea is by no means limited to the case of finite groups, but the theory in that case is particularly well-behaved.</p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwFQ" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwFg" aria-labelledby="Constructions"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Constructions">Constructions</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Induced_representation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Constructions"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwFw" aria-labelledby="Algebraic"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Algebraic">Algebraic</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Induced_representation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Algebraic"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt8" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwGA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Representation theory of finite groups#The induced representation"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1368532237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt9" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt8" id="mwGQ">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Representation_theory_of_finite_groups#The_induced_representation" title="Representation theory of finite groups">Representation theory of finite groups §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>The induced representation</a></div>
<p id="mwGg">Let <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt10" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwGw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> be a finite group and <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt11" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwHA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span> any subgroup of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt12" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwHQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span>.  Furthermore let <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt13" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwHg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"(&apos;&apos;π&apos;&apos;, &apos;&apos;V&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'>(<i>π</i>, <i>V</i>)</span> be a representation of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt14" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwHw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span>.  Let <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt15" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwIA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;n&apos;&apos; {{=}} [&apos;&apos;G&apos;&apos; : &apos;&apos;H&apos;&apos;]"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>n</i> = [<i>G</i><span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>: <i>H</i>]</span> be the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Index_of_a_subgroup" title="Index of a subgroup" id="mwIQ">index</a> of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt16" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwIg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span> in <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt17" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwIw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> and let <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt18" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwJA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;g&apos;&apos;&lt;sub>1&lt;/sub>, ..., &apos;&apos;g&lt;sub>n&lt;/sub>&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>g</i><sub>1</sub>, ..., <i>g<sub>n</sub></i></span> be a full set of representatives in <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt19" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwJQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coset" title="Coset" id="mwJg">left cosets</a> in <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt20" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwJw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;G&apos;&apos;/&apos;&apos;H&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>G</i>/<i>H</i></span>. The induced representation <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt21" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Ind{{su|b=&apos;&apos;H&apos;&apos;|p=&apos;&apos;G&apos;&apos;}} &apos;&apos;π&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'>Ind<span class="nowrap"><span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:-0.3em;vertical-align:-0.4em;line-height:1.2em;font-size:80%;text-align:left"><sup style="font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline"><i>G</i></sup><br/><sub style="font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline"><i>H</i></sub></span></span> <i>π</i></span> can be thought of as acting on the following space:</p>

<dl id="mwKQ"><dd id="mwKg"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt22" id="mwKw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"W=\\bigoplus_{i=1}^n g_i V."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle W=\bigoplus _{i=1}^{n}g_{i}V.}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>W</mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <munderover>
          <mo>⨁<!-- ⨁ --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
            <mo>=</mo>
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </munderover>
        <msub>
          <mi>g</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mi>V</mi>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle W=\bigoplus _{i=1}^{n}g_{i}V.}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f35c6cc07549a0909a5bc7cd6be025051b82b054" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -3.005ex; width:13.774ex; height:6.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle W=\bigoplus _{i=1}^{n}g_{i}V.}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwLA">Here each <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt23" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;g&lt;sub>i&lt;/sub>&amp;thinsp;V&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>g<sub>i</sub><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>V</i></span> is an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isomorphic" title="Isomorphic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLg">isomorphic</a> copy of the vector space <i id="mwLw">V</i> whose elements are written as <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt24" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwMA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;g&lt;sub>i&lt;/sub>&amp;thinsp;v&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>g<sub>i</sub><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>v</i></span> with <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt25" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwMQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;v&apos;&apos; &amp;isin; &apos;&apos;V&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>v</i> <span typeof="mw:Entity">∈</span> <i>V</i></span>. For each <i id="mwMg">g</i> in <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt26" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwMw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> there is an <i id="mwNA">h<sub id="mwNQ">i</sub></i> in <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt27" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwNg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span> for each <i id="mwNw">i</i> and a permutation <i id="mwOA">j</i> of {1, ..., <i id="mwOQ">n</i>} such that  <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt28" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwOg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;math&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Math&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;''g'' ''g&lt;sub>i&lt;/sub>'' = ''g''&lt;sub>''j''(''i'')&lt;/sub> ''h&lt;sub>i&lt;/sub>''&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i>g</i> <i>g<sub>i</sub></i> = <i>g</i><sub><i>j</i>(<i>i</i>)</sub> <i>h<sub>i</sub></i></span>, where <i id="mwOw">h<sub id="mwPA">i</sub></i> as well as <i id="mwPQ">j</i> depend on <i id="mwPg">g</i>. This is just another way of saying that <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt29" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwPw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;g&apos;&apos;&lt;sub>1&lt;/sub>, ..., &apos;&apos;g&lt;sub>n&lt;/sub>&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>g</i><sub>1</sub>, ..., <i>g<sub>n</sub></i></span> is a full set of representatives. Via the induced representation <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt30" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwQA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> acts on <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt31" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwQQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"W"}},"i":0}}]}'>W</span> as follows:</p>

<dl id="mwQg"><dd id="mwQw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt32" id="mwRA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":" g\\cdot\\sum_{i=1}^n g_i v_i=\\sum_{i=1}^n g_{j(i)} \\pi(h_i) v_i"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle g\cdot \sum _{i=1}^{n}g_{i}v_{i}=\sum _{i=1}^{n}g_{j(i)}\pi (h_{i})v_{i}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>g</mi>
        <mo>⋅<!-- ⋅ --></mo>
        <munderover>
          <mo>∑<!-- ∑ --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
            <mo>=</mo>
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </munderover>
        <msub>
          <mi>g</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <msub>
          <mi>v</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <munderover>
          <mo>∑<!-- ∑ --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
            <mo>=</mo>
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </munderover>
        <msub>
          <mi>g</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>j</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
            <mi>i</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mi>π<!-- π --></mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>h</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>v</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle g\cdot \sum _{i=1}^{n}g_{i}v_{i}=\sum _{i=1}^{n}g_{j(i)}\pi (h_{i})v_{i}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9f686ed842f332c15aa8bb11c842ee55daaa9ce1" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -3.005ex; width:28.287ex; height:6.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle g\cdot \sum _{i=1}^{n}g_{i}v_{i}=\sum _{i=1}^{n}g_{j(i)}\pi (h_{i})v_{i}}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwRQ">where <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt33" id="mwRg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":" v_i \\in V"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle v_{i}\in V}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>v</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>∈<!-- ∈ --></mo>
        <mi>V</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle v_{i}\in V}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/314467aba70c6bd74cacc52d232baacce36f80ad" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:6.555ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle v_{i}\in V}"/></span> for each <i id="mwRw">i</i>.</p>

<p id="mwSA">Alternatively, one can construct induced representations by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Change_of_rings#Extension_of_scalars" title="Change of rings" id="mwSQ">extension of scalars</a>: any <i id="mwSg">K-</i>linear representation <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt34" id="mwSw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\pi"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \pi }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>π<!-- π --></mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \pi }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9be4ba0bb8df3af72e90a0535fabcc17431e540a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.332ex; height:1.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \pi }"/></span>  of the group <i id="mwTA">H</i> can be viewed as a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Module_(mathematics)" title="Module (mathematics)" id="mwTQ">module</a> <i id="mwTg">V</i> over the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_ring" title="Group ring" id="mwTw">group ring</a> <i id="mwUA">K</i>[<i id="mwUQ">H</i>]. We can then define</p>

<dl id="mwUg"><dd id="mwUw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt35" id="mwVA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\operatorname{Ind}_H^G\\pi= K[G]\\otimes_{K[H]} V."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Ind} _{H}^{G}\pi =K[G]\otimes _{K[H]}V.}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>Ind</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>H</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>G</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo>⁡<!-- ⁡ --></mo>
        <mi>π<!-- π --></mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mi>K</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
        <mi>G</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
        <msub>
          <mo>⊗<!-- ⊗ --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>K</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
            <mi>H</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mi>V</mi>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \operatorname {Ind} _{H}^{G}\pi =K[G]\otimes _{K[H]}V.}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/4c6c6e39f096b4dabbe5ba5b520f05fec96bdcc2" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.171ex; width:24.462ex; height:3.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Ind} _{H}^{G}\pi =K[G]\otimes _{K[H]}V.}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwVQ">This latter formula can also be used to define <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt36" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwVg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Ind{{su|b=&apos;&apos;H&apos;&apos;|p=&apos;&apos;G&apos;&apos;}} &apos;&apos;π&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'>Ind<span class="nowrap"><span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:-0.3em;vertical-align:-0.4em;line-height:1.2em;font-size:80%;text-align:left"><sup style="font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline"><i>G</i></sup><br/><sub style="font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline"><i>H</i></sub></span></span> <i>π</i></span> for any group <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt37" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwVw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> and subgroup <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt38" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwWA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span>, without requiring any finiteness.<sup about="#mwt39" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-1" id="mwWQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwXQ" aria-labelledby="Examples"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Examples">Examples</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Induced_representation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Examples"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwXg">For any group, the induced representation of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trivial_representation" title="Trivial representation" id="mwXw">trivial representation</a> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trivial_subgroup" title="Trivial subgroup" class="mw-redirect" id="mwYA">trivial subgroup</a> is the right <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regular_representation" title="Regular representation" id="mwYQ">regular representation</a>.  More generally the induced representation of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trivial_representation" title="Trivial representation" id="mwYg">trivial representation</a> of any subgroup is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Permutation_representation" title="Permutation representation" id="mwYw">permutation representation</a> on the cosets of that subgroup.</p>

<p id="mwZA">An induced representation of a one-dimensional representation is called a <b id="mwZQ">monomial representation</b>, because it can be represented as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monomial_matrix" title="Monomial matrix" class="mw-redirect" id="mwZg">monomial matrices</a>.  Some groups have the property that all of their irreducible representations are monomial, the so-called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monomial_group" title="Monomial group" id="mwZw">monomial groups</a>.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwaA" aria-labelledby="Properties"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Properties">Properties</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Induced_representation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Properties"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwaQ">If <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt40" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwag" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span> is a subgroup of the group <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt41" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwaw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span>, then every <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt42" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwbA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"K"}},"i":0}}]}'>K</span>-linear representation <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt43" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwbQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ρ"}},"i":0}}]}'>ρ</span> of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt44" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwbg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> can be viewed as a <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt45" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwbw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"K"}},"i":0}}]}'>K</span>-linear representation of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt46" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwcA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span>; this is known as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Restricted_representation" title="Restricted representation" id="mwcQ">restriction</a> of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt47" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwcg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ρ"}},"i":0}}]}'>ρ</span> to <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt48" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwcw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span> and denoted by <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt49" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwdA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Res(&amp;rho;)"}},"i":0}}]}'>Res(<span typeof="mw:Entity">ρ</span>)</span>. In the case of finite groups and finite-dimensional representations, the <b id="mwdQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frobenius_reciprocity" title="Frobenius reciprocity" id="mwdg">Frobenius reciprocity theorem</a></b> states that, given representations <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt50" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwdw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"σ"}},"i":0}}]}'>σ</span> of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt51" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mweA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span> and <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt52" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mweQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ρ"}},"i":0}}]}'>ρ</span> of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt53" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mweg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span>, the space of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt54" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwew" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span>-<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equivariant" title="Equivariant" class="mw-redirect" id="mwfA">equivariant</a> linear maps from <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt55" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwfQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"σ"}},"i":0}}]}'>σ</span> to <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt56" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwfg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Res(&apos;&apos;ρ&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'>Res(<i>ρ</i>)</span> has the same dimension over <i id="mwfw">K</i> as that of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt57" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwgA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span>-equivariant linear maps from <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt58" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwgQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Ind(&apos;&apos;σ&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'>Ind(<i>σ</i>)</span> to <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt59" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwgg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ρ"}},"i":0}}]}'>ρ</span>.<sup about="#mwt63" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwgw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwhA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwhw">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_property" title="Universal property" id="mwiA">universal property</a> of the induced representation, which is also valid for infinite groups, is equivalent to the adjunction asserted in the reciprocity theorem. If <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt69" id="mwiQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"(\\sigma,V)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle (\sigma ,V)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mi>V</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle (\sigma ,V)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1f8cfc26bba796d23adc325c86aab79747358798" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:5.96ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle (\sigma ,V)}"/></span> is a representation of <i id="mwig">H</i> and <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt70" id="mwiw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"(\\operatorname{Ind}(\\sigma),\\hat{V})"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle (\operatorname {Ind} (\sigma ),{\hat {V}})}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>Ind</mi>
        <mo>⁡<!-- ⁡ --></mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mover>
              <mi>V</mi>
              <mo stretchy="false">^<!-- ^ --></mo>
            </mover>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle (\operatorname {Ind} (\sigma ),{\hat {V}})}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/303a5d58cf2586721522a7dda2c874671f80bb43" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:11.194ex; height:3.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle (\operatorname {Ind} (\sigma ),{\hat {V}})}"/></span> is the representation of <i id="mwjA">G</i> induced by <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt71" id="mwjQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\sigma"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \sigma }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \sigma }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/59f59b7c3e6fdb1d0365a494b81fb9a696138c36" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.33ex; height:1.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \sigma }"/></span>, then there exists a <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt64" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwjg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span>-equivariant linear map <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt72" id="mwjw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"j:V\\to\\hat{V}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle j:V\to {\hat {V}}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
