  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/28ad75d2997d7b5ad7ef656cfec4626421adc495" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -2.505ex; width:26.492ex; height:6.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\widehat {\chi }}(k)={\begin{cases}\chi (k)&amp;{\text{if }}k\in H\\0&amp;{\text{otherwise}}\end{cases}}}"/></span></dd></dl>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwsQ" aria-labelledby="Analytic"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Analytic">Analytic</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Induced_representation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Analytic"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwsg">If <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt89" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwsw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locally_compact" title="Locally compact" class="mw-redirect" id="mwtA">locally compact</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topological_group" title="Topological group" id="mwtQ">topological group</a> (possibly infinite) and <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt90" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwtg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Closed_set" title="Closed set" id="mwtw">closed</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subgroup" title="Subgroup" id="mwuA">subgroup</a> then there is a common analytic construction of the induced representation.  Let <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt91" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwuQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"(&apos;&apos;π&apos;&apos;, &apos;&apos;V&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'>(<i>π</i>, <i>V</i>)</span> be a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Continuous_function" title="Continuous function" id="mwug">continuous</a> unitary representation of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt92" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwuw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H"}},"i":0}}]}'>H</span> into a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilbert_space" title="Hilbert space" id="mwvA">Hilbert space</a> <i id="mwvQ">V</i>.  We can then let:</p>

<dl id="mwvg"><dd id="mwvw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt93" id="mwwA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\operatorname{Ind}_H^G\\pi= \\left\\{\\phi\\colon G \\to V \\ : \\ \\phi(gh^{-1})=\\pi(h)\\phi(g)\\text{ for all }h\\in H,\\; g\\in G \\text{ and } \\ \\phi \\in L^2(G/H)\\right\\}."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Ind} _{H}^{G}\pi =\left\{\phi \colon G\to V\ :\ \phi (gh^{-1})=\pi (h)\phi (g){\text{ for all }}h\in H,\;g\in G{\text{ and }}\ \phi \in L^{2}(G/H)\right\}.}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
