        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \operatorname {Ind} _{H}^{G}\pi =\left\{\phi \colon G\to V\</annotation></semantics></math><span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>:\ \phi (gh^{-1})=\pi (h)\phi (g){\text{ for all }}h\in H,\;g\in G{\text{ and }}\ \phi \in L^{2}(G/H)\right\}.}
  
</span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/296606ba4bbbda5904cda6e5579c7b5afd8ec681" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:86.2ex; height:3.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Ind} _{H}^{G}\pi =\left\{\phi \colon G\to V\ :\ \phi (gh^{-1})=\pi (h)\phi (g){\text{ for all }}h\in H,\;g\in G{\text{ and }}\ \phi \in L^{2}(G/H)\right\}.}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwwQ">Here <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt94" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwwg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;phi;&amp;isin;&apos;&apos;L&apos;&apos;&lt;sup>2&lt;/sup>(&apos;&apos;G&apos;&apos;/&apos;&apos;H&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'><span typeof="mw:Entity">φ</span><span typeof="mw:Entity">∈</span><i>L</i><sup>2</sup>(<i>G</i>/<i>H</i>)</span> means: the space <i id="mwww">G</i>/<i id="mwxA">H</i> carries a suitable invariant measure, and since the norm of  <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt95" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwxQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;phi;(&apos;&apos;g&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'><span typeof="mw:Entity">φ</span>(<i>g</i>)</span>  is constant on each left coset of <i id="mwxg">H</i>, we can integrate the square of these norms over <i id="mwxw">G</i>/<i id="mwyA">H</i> and obtain a finite result.  The group <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt96" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwyQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"G"}},"i":0}}]}'>G</span> acts on the induced representation space by translation, that is, <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt97" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwyg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"(&apos;&apos;g&apos;&apos;.&amp;phi;)(&apos;&apos;x&apos;&apos;)=&amp;phi;(&apos;&apos;g&apos;&apos;&lt;sup>−1&lt;/sup>&apos;&apos;x&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'>(<i>g</i>.<span typeof="mw:Entity">φ</span>)(<i>x</i>)=<span typeof="mw:Entity">φ</span>(<i>g</i><sup>−1</sup><i>x</i>)</span> for <i id="mwyw">g,x</i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwzA">∈</span><i id="mwzQ">G</i> and <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt98" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwzg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;phi;&amp;isin;Ind{{su|b=&apos;&apos;H&apos;&apos;|p=&apos;&apos;G&apos;&apos;}} &apos;&apos;π&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><span typeof="mw:Entity">φ</span><span typeof="mw:Entity">∈</span>Ind<span class="nowrap"><span style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:-0.3em;vertical-align:-0.4em;line-height:1.2em;font-size:80%;text-align:left"><sup style="font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline"><i>G</i></sup><br/><sub style="font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline"><i>H</i></sub></span></span> <i>π</i></span>.</p>

<p id="mwzw">This construction is often modified in various ways to fit the applications needed.  A common version is called <b id="mw0A">normalized induction</b> and usually uses the same notation.  The definition of the representation space is as follows:</p>

<dl id="mw0Q"><dd id="mw0g"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt99" id="mw0w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\operatorname{Ind}_H^G\\pi= \\left \\{\\phi \\colon G \\to V \\ : \\  \\phi(gh^{-1})=\\Delta_G^{-\\frac{1}{2}}(h)\\Delta_H^{\\frac{1}{2}}(h)\\pi(h)\\phi(g)  \\text{ and }  \\phi\\in L^2(G/H) \\right \\}."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Ind} _{H}^{G}\pi =\left\{\phi \colon G\to V\ :\ \phi (gh^{-1})=\Delta _{G}^{-{\frac {1}{2}}}(h)\Delta _{H}^{\frac {1}{2}}(h)\pi (h)\phi (g){\text{ and }}\phi \in L^{2}(G/H)\right\}.}">
  <semantics>
